# The ct.sym of javac on Arbace's --release N, Arbace's own (JCS50 (b), JCS50-1 (a); doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md,
# "As built: JCS50 (b), the own ct.sym"): made by the JDK build's CreateSymbols (jdk26u at baf63fbe42b8758448fee570a9d9bb914272d259,
# make/langtools/src/classes/build/tools/symbolgenerator/CreateSymbols.java), read by repr/java and interpreted on javac's tool,
# over src/jdk.compiler/share/data/symbols and the own platform's modules (jdk/javac/platform.sha256) with their exploded
# descriptors, with the build's arguments jdk/javac/ct-sym-build.edn (test/javac-platform/ctsym.bash; bin/javac-vendor ct-sym-own);
# its SHA-256, equal to the JDK build's images/jdk/lib/ct.sym's (ct-sym-oracle). Kept in the own platform's cache, linked into the
# platform beside the modules as DIR/ct.sym. Apart from platform.sha256, whose digest keys the own platform's cache.
# kind: own
642d31ba38e4b2222b1992206863983e87fdc529d99ee4fe2d6b77c7d31ba6f4  ct.sym
